{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/714260-mortal-remains-demon-hunting-factions-a-retrospecive","id":714260,"title":"Mortal Remains: Demon Hunting factions, a retrospecive","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-22T06:01:36-07:00","id":714260,"title":"Mortal Remains: Demon Hunting factions, a retrospecive","content":"So this is sort of about &quot;Utopia Now&quot; and &quot;The knights of St Adrian&quot;. In both cases, I don't get it? I'm not opposed to more factions in WoD but... <br /> <br /> Why the Knights? wouldn't it have been easier to simply allow the players to become employees of Deva corporation? seems like it would have a similar effect.<br /> <br /> Secondly, I get Utopia Now, but in a completely different vein that this slot could have filled, why are none of the groups hunting Angels and the God Machine (circle back to Deva)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T07:27:44-07:00","id":714464,"title":"","content":"On Utopia Now-Actually, they do hunt Angels and the God Machine, as much as they do devils. They don't discriminate.<br /> <br /> On the Knights of Saint Adrian, It's because ...Look, I'm going to quote myself, because I'm lazy, and then add in a little something on Deva<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a few reasons for the love. First off is that it is a very bold and upfront conspiracy, even if the 80s action hero <i>is</i> somewhat taking it too far. They don't have a complex motivation for what they do-they're demons and it's a paycheck and it's much like hunting down any other criminal as a bounty hunter, a certain bluntness is needed. The way they approach their jobs as hunter, as dictated by the Ink Endowment, is similarly blunt-three of the eight directly tie into brawl and require, you know, actually hitting someone(although the third one, LOVE/HATE, has a twofer purpose, and only one is violent), with a fourth one that basically makes you as superior in some trait(Namely-Strength, Dexterity, Brawl, Weaponry, Firearms) as the last guy you fought. They can have a certain amount of infinite resources in regards to firearms and vehicles, which invites reckless use thereof-you can totally smash a car into a building and not worry about it. The remaining ones might be....subtler? But it's just a refreshingly straightforward group with a no-nonsense attitude that, mixed in with a bit of vicious cunning, is very effective.<br /> <br /> That bluntness might not be so appealing...if it wasn't for the fact that <i>their enemies are demons</i> and that it <i>actually works</i>. Something this unsubtle shouldn't even be able to touch the Unchained(or your world's equivalent), but all it takes it one hit to start some serious momentum<br /> <br /> I'm not saying they can't be smart, or cunning-on the contrary, I think a lot of them actually are. They are, after all, bounty hunters, probably for normal criminals in between the demons as well. But when they take the stage, when they act, it's with the zeal of angels without the stigma of religious culture-rather, their zeal might seem angelic for its' potency, but it's born from road culture, bar fights, and a general salt of the earth background.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they went with Deva, they'd play the same spy games that Demons and Angels play. That's boring because it looks like everything else. The Sidearms are refreshing because they are a great example of when and how a &quot;cut through the bullshit&quot; mentality will work, bringing in a new dynamic to the game of demons and angels that keeps everyone on their toes.<br /> <br /> It's like nitro, in short.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T07:39:01-07:00","id":714484,"title":"","content":"Watsonian answer for Utopia Now: because they are a Hunter group for specifically targeting a Player group. Each of the other groups are tailor made to be problems for player splats. Players don't play as Angels, so...<br /> <br /> Though from the write-up, Utopia Now also tangles with G-M Angels as well. They really can't tell the difference, and parts are parts.<br /> <br /> As for the Knights of St. Adrian... I got nothing. I found them to be the least interesting/plausible of Hunter groups (even over the two hippie groups). Deva Corp would indeed have been a better option. Maybe they didn't want to step on the themes of The Cheiron Group?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T07:42:30-07:00","id":714505,"title":"","content":"I have no idea if you guys are American or not, so let me just say that the Sidearms tap into a cultural vein on the subject of faith that Demon deals with that is both directly what it talks about on that subject and yet still quite sideways to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T17:32:26-07:00","id":716350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/714260-mortal-remains-demon-hunting-factions-a-retrospecive?p=714505#post714505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Sidearms tap into a cultural vein on the subject of faith that Demon deals with that is both directly what it talks about on that subject and yet still quite sideways to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean the Knights of Saint Adrian, yes? How do they really tap into faith, from your assessment? From their write-up, I mostly got the impression that most of them were merely mercenary. Their &quot;don't ask questions&quot; wasn't any kind of faith, but more a &quot;I'm not being paid to ask them. I <b>am</b> being paid to do what I enjoy anyways.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}